WEBVTT

00:00:00.961 --> 00:00:03.631
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Five couples left London at the start of the race,

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:08.963
and one was eliminated during the journey, leaving four to cross the finish line in Singapore.

00:00:09.566 --> 00:00:15.856
The couples had travelled by train, bus, boat, and taxi, through mountains, deserts, and tropical islands.

00:00:16.101 --> 00:00:19.167
They had worked in farms, flower shops, hostels,

00:00:19.194 --> 00:00:24.148
and animal sanctuaries on their journeys, exploring different cultures, taking risks,

00:00:24.265 --> 00:00:25.820
and confronting their fears.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:30.718
The eventual winners were 61-year-old retired teachers Tony and Elaine,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.442
who claimed the £20,000 prize money.

00:00:33.978 --> 00:00:38.448
Natalie and Shameema finished third overall and Josh and Felix last

00:00:38.663 --> 00:00:41.228
– they didn’t have enough money to reach the final checkpoint,

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:45.532
but were given the money by Natalie and Shameema so that they could complete the race.

00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:49.909
The contestants remember relying on people’s help, laughing,

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:55.044
connecting without a common language, feeling exhausted, despondent, and jubilant,

00:00:55.384 --> 00:01:00.602
finding their courage, and discovering that if you show respect, kindness is universal.

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:04.898
The ‘loveliest moments’, they all say, were chatting with people on trains

00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:09.864
– tales of hair-plaiting, exchanging chocolate for chicken, sharing photos,

00:01:09.923 --> 00:01:11.727
the gesture of a hand on heart.

00:01:12.649 --> 00:01:14.504
The teams returned home in December.

00:01:15.048 --> 00:01:19.341
Before jumping back into work, Josh and Felix took a holiday with their girlfriends.

00:01:19.585 --> 00:01:22.055
Natalie went on a month’s silent meditation.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:29.128
Shameema enrolled in a boxing class and won a match in front of 1,000 people (including her daughters and Natalie).

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:35.084
Josh recalls that at first the production crew tried to ‘gee up’ the competitive side of the race,

00:01:35.109 --> 00:01:41.869
but soon, he says, ‘They realized it was about the human stories. It’s always about the human stories.’